21. In view of the aforementioned, the following:
ORDER i) The appeal is allowed in part;
 ii) The judgment and award dated 21.10.2016  passed in MVC No.1175/2015 by the IV Additional District Judge and Member MACT, D.K, Mangaluru, is modified to the extent of holding that the claimants shall be entitled to a further compensation of `1,62,330/- together with interest at 7% p.a., from the date of petition till date of payment in addition to the compensation awarded by the Tribunal.

In all other respects, the judgment and award of the Tribunal remains unaltered;
iii) The insurer shall deposit the compensation awarded together with accrued interest within six weeks;
iv) The enhanced compensation together with accrued interest shall be digitally released in - 11 - NC: 2025:KHC:25652 HC-KAR favour of the claimants in terms of the award of the Tribunal;
v) The Registry to draw the modified award accordingly;
Mrs Pushpa vs Mr Manikanta on 10 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/97875938/

